        "richtext_PAANig": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Age-related diseases and symptoms happen faster when you are not getting enough omega-3s in your diet. When consuming enough long-chain omega-3s, one notices improvement in heart rate variability, lowered heart rate and blood pressure, improved endothelial function (lining of the blood vessels), decreased platelet aggregation, and lowered blood triglyceride levels. So, how much is enough?</p><p>The American Heart Association recommends two weekly servings of fatty fish to maintain an appropriate source for the diet. However, research findings are showing that this amount may not be enough to maintain optimal amounts of omega-3’s to reap the amazing benefits now proven in numerous studies. Most current studies utilize up to three times this amount for effective dosages that can optimize these numerous benefits for the body. OMEGA+++ is available in a 120-count bottle so you can take 3 daily as needed.<br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
